{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xv", "label": "Article XV \u2014 Shared and personal are separate layers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_14_federation_goal_p1", "label": "14 \u00a7P1 \u2014 Independent mirrors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "label": "Stage 28 \u2014 Export and import a claim, a topic, or an outline (planned, not started)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Planned, not built. Federation is not being built here, but a file is the smallest thing that delivers 14 \u00a7P1's mirrors and \u00a7P2's partial nodes: a mirror is a node that imported one. It is also the answer to a question the project cannot currently answer a contributor \u2014 can I have my work back, in a form that outlives this server? Work no one can carry out of the building is not cumulative (Article XXI)."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_full_vs_compact", "label": "Full is mirrored, Compact is re-asserted by the importer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A foreign contribution cannot join this node's chain: splicing someone else's entries would break ledger:verify for everyone. Full arrives with its original signatures, verifiable against the origin's keys, kept verbatim as mirrored entries. Compact carries no signatures, so attributing it to the named authors would be a forgery this system would then publish as fact; it therefore creates new local contributions signed by the importer with derived_from. The failure is silent and permanent \u2014 a graph full of claims apparently signed by people who never saw them \u2014 so acceptance test 5 exists to catch it."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_closure", "label": "The closure \u2014 where a claim's file stops", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The graph has no natural edge, so it must be decided before anything is written. Inference premises are referenced by id and not followed, or a single claim drags in the graph; an unresolved reference is marked external with its origin so a reader can tell a boundary from an omission."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_withheld_and_personal", "label": "Moderation is visible in the counts; the personal layer never leaves", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Quarantined and taken-down material is not exported and counts.withheld says how many entries were held back with the log entry that did it \u2014 a silent gap would be worse than a visible one (Article XIII). Personal assessments, affiliations, users, sessions and tokens appear in neither profile (Article XV), asserted by a test rather than left as a convention."}, {"id": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_deterministic_bundle", "label": "eir-export-v1 \u2014 a byte-identical, node-signed bundle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "bundle_hash is over the body in RFC 8785 canonical form and the header is signed by the system key following eir-checkpoint-v1, so a mirror can tell a file came from the node it names, intact, without asking that node anything, and two nodes holding one subject can be compared by hash. Compact states verifiable: false in its own header, because a reader who cannot check something should be told by the file rather than by a footnote."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_full_vs_compact", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_closure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_withheld_and_personal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "target": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_deterministic_bundle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_deterministic_bundle", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_23_federation_ready_checkpoint", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_full_vs_compact", "target": "app_services_ledger_apply_apply", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_deterministic_bundle", "target": "app_services_crypto_canonical_json_canonicaljson", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_deterministic_bundle", "target": "app_services_snapshots_checkpoint_checkpoint", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_stage", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_14_federation_goal_p1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage_28_export_import_withheld_and_personal", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xv", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/planned/stage-28-export-import.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_planned_stage